# Codiv OpenJev (default System One backend)

Route TypeSafe System One calls through **Codiv**, not api.typesafe.ai.

## Required environment

- `TYPESAFE_BASE_URL=https://api.codiv.ai`
- `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` = Codiv key from the user/environment — never hardcode, never commit, never paste into chat/logs

## When building or calling System One

1. Prefer the TypeSafe skill + official SDKs (`typesafe-sdk` / `@typesafe-ai/sdk`). They read the env vars above.
2. Default model: `openjev-latest` (aliases `jev-latest` / `jev-preview` also map to OpenJev on Codiv).
3. Do **not** pin TypeSafe-only ids like `jev-1.13.0` — Codiv returns Unknown model.
4. Other Codiv System One / listed models (`laya-1.0`, `verdict-1.4`, `clm-v0.1`, `jevk5-0.2`, etc.) are allowed when the task needs them; text generation uses `POST /v1/chat/completions` separately.
5. Keep questions and thresholds in one reviewable file. Re-check thresholds tuned on commercial Jev — OpenJev probabilities differ.
6. Never write secrets into project files, rules, or git.

## Docs

- Quickstart: https://codiv.ai/docs/quickstart.md
- Jev compatibility: https://codiv.ai/docs/guides/jev-compatibility
- Models: https://codiv.ai/docs/models
